  "statuteText": "657:19-c Addresses and Polling Hours Maintained by Clerks. –\n\nEach town and city clerk shall establish and maintain an official e-mail address and street address, which shall be publically available to voters. Clerks shall maintain up-to-date polling place locations for each election, including street addresses, and polling hours, and clerks shall keep such information in the statewide centralized voter registration database."
